## Overview

Product Education Specialists at Precisely design and deliver modern learning and user assistance experiences that help users get the most value from our products. As part of a global User Assistance team, you work closely with Engineering, Product Management, Product Marketing, Customer Support, and other cross-functional stakeholders in an Agile and AI-first environment.

You lead the evolution of product education toward modern, in-product and self-service experiences that empower end users to successfully achieve their goals. Moving beyond traditional training models, you design contextual, just-in-time guidance that supports users in the flow of work — helping them complete key tasks faster, increasing adoption, reducing time-to-value, and enhancing the overall product experience.

---

## What You Will Do

- Lead and define the strategy and roadmap for evolving product education from traditional training and documentation to modern, in-product and self-service experiences, including defining what successful product adoption looks like for end users.
- Drive a shift toward modern learning experiences, including in-product guidance, contextual help, and AI-powered self-service via Help Center, search, and chat.
- Design task-based, workflow-driven learning that enables users to successfully complete key actions in the product.
- Partner with Product, UX, and Engineering to drive end-to-end education and user assistance experiences across the product, with a strong ability to work cross-functionally and lead initiatives across teams.
- Define and implement a scalable self-service learning strategy across Help Center, Knowledge Base, documentation, and internal sources.
- Ensure a unified and seamless learning experience across channels, so users can access consistent, connected information regardless of where they are in their journey.
- Continuously measure and improve learning effectiveness using data, feedback, and user behavior insights tied to adoption and user success.
- Other duties may be assigned.

---

## What We Are Looking For

- Bachelor's degree in a related field such as Communications, Education, Instructional Design, Marketing, Computer Science, or a related discipline (or equivalent experience)
- 8+ years of experience in product education, user assistance, learning and development, instructional design, technical communications, or a closely related field
- Strong sense of ownership and curiosity, with a demonstrated eagerness to stay ahead of trends in product education, learning technologies, and AI-driven experiences
- Experience designing modern, AI-enabled education and user assistance experiences, leveraging tools such as Microsoft Copilot, GitHub Copilot, Azure OpenAI, and AI-driven content platforms to build in-product guidance, conversational assistants, and scalable self-service solutions powered by RAG-based retrieval, prompt-driven workflows, and structured knowledge systems
- Proven track record of strong project management and communication skills to successfully lead cross-functional initiatives
- Proven experience designing role-based learning programs using adult learning principles and instructional design frameworks (ADDIE, SAM)
- Strong understanding of how adults learn in the flow of work, with the ability to design task-based, just-in-time learning experiences that prioritize action over content consumption
- Hands-on experience with learning and content tools, including:
  - **Learning management systems:** Docebo, SAP Litmos, Cornerstone
  - **Authoring tools:** EasyGenerator, Articulate, Camtasia, Adobe Captivate
  - **Video creation tools:** Camtasia, Guidde, Loom, Adobe Premiere Pro or similar
  - **Knowledge platforms:** SharePoint, Confluence

